      "content": "thanks. it looks good but i'm a bit worried it's too soft. these corporate lawyers are going to try and claim the rights lapsed or that the trust wasn't properly filed in the 80s. can we add a section that mentions the precedent of the undisclosed family shareholder agreements? i want to make it clear that if they ignore this, I'll be forced to move toward litigation to secure the assets that belong to my lineage. make it sound a bit more... intimidating? like i actually have the legal standing to freeze their current distribution of these assets.",
